---
const title = "Privacy Notice | Test Before You Build";
const description =
  "How Test Before You Build handles the personal information submitted through this website.";
const canonical = "https://testbeforeyoubuild.com/privacy/";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <a href="/">← Test Before You Build</a>
      <a href="/about-kari-jaaskelainen/">About Dr. Kari</a>
    </header>
    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This notice explains how personal data is processed when you use the
        Test Before You Build website or contact us through its form.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller and contact</h2>
      <p>
        The controller is Kari Jääskeläinen, operating the Test Before You Build
        service. Privacy enquiries and requests can be submitted through the
        <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>. Please write “Privacy request” at
        the beginning of the message. No data protection officer has been
        appointed because the processing does not require one.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Personal data we process</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact us, we process the information you provide: your name,
        email address, description of your idea, and information you provide
        about the intended customer or problem. Some forms may require these
        details so that we can assess the enquiry. We may also process subsequent
        correspondence and information needed to manage a potential customer
        relationship. Please do not include trade secrets, health information,
        or other sensitive personal data in the form.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
      <p>
        We use enquiry data to respond to you, assess whether the service is a
        suitable fit, prepare possible next steps, and take measures at your
        request before entering into a contract. The legal basis is Article
        6(1)(b) GDPR. Where an enquiry is made on behalf of an organisation, we
        also rely on our legitimate interest under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR in
        communicating with potential customers and developing our business.
      </p>
      <p>
        We process limited technical data where necessary to operate, secure,
        and troubleshoot the website. This is based on our legitimate interest
        under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR in providing a secure and reliable service.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand aggregate website usage
        and page performance. According to Cloudflare, Web Analytics does not
        use cookies, local storage, cross-site tracking, or fingerprinting and
        does not collect or use visitors’ personal data. We do not use
        advertising cookies or behavioural profiling on this website.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Service providers, recipients, and transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions are processed by Formspree, Inc. as our service
        provider. Cloudflare, Inc. provides website delivery, security, and Web
        Analytics services. Relevant data may also be handled by our email and
        hosting service providers. We do not sell personal data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Formspree and Cloudflare are headquartered in the United States, so
        processing may involve transfers outside the European Economic Area.
        Where required, these transfers are protected by the European
        Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses and other applicable
        safeguards. Information about the providers’ safeguards is available in
        the <a href="https://formspree.io/security/">Formspree security information</a>
        and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/trust-hub/gdpr/">Cloudflare GDPR information</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not lead to a customer relationship are deleted or
        anonymised no later than 12 months after the last communication. If a
        customer relationship begins, relevant information may be retained for
        the duration of that relationship and afterwards only as long as needed
        for accounting, legal claims, or other statutory obligations. Technical
        data is retained according to the applicable service provider’s retention
        settings and only for as long as necessary for security and operation.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to the conditions of the GDPR, you may request access to your
        personal data, correction or deletion of it, restriction of processing,
        and data portability. You may object to processing based on legitimate
        interests. To exercise these rights, use the
        <a href="/#contact">contact form</a> and identify the request as a privacy
        matter. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
        authority. In Finland, the authority is the
        <a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en/home">Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Is providing data mandatory?</h2>
      <p>
        Providing personal data is voluntary and is not a statutory or
        contractual requirement. However, we need your name, email address, and
        a description of your idea to assess and respond to your enquiry. If you
        do not provide them, we cannot respond through the form.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Automated decision-making</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use personal data submitted through the website for automated
        decision-making or profiling, and we do not use form submissions to train
        AI models.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this notice if the website, our processing activities, or
        legal requirements change. The latest version and its update date are
        published on this page.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: 11 September 2026</p>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <a href="/">Return to the homepage</a>
      <a href="/about-kari-jaaskelainen/">About Dr. Kari</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    color: #0d1930;
    background: #f5f8fc;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; }
  header, main, footer { width: min(760px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; }
  header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; padding: 30px 0; }
  main { margin-top: 28px; padding: 48px; border: 1px solid #d8e0ec; border-radius: 24px; background: #fff; }
  footer { display: flex; gap: 24px; padding: 30px 0 50px; }
  a { color: #155eef; font-weight: 750; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 12px; color: #155eef; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.4rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  h2 { margin: 36px 0 8px; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  p { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #536781; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.18rem; color: #405573; }
  .updated { margin-top: 40px; font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { main { padding: 30px 24px; } }
</style>
